  "content": {
    "title": "Dan Levy’s New Netflix Series 'Big Mistakes' Features a Stacked Cast",
    "text": "Courtesy of NetflixDan Levy as NickyDan Levy anchors the series as Nicky, a gay pastor suddenly thrown into criminal chaos. Anxious, overthinking, and deeply unqualified for a life of crime, Nicky is essentially Levy’s worst-case scenario personified.Best known for co-creating and starring in the Emmy-winning series Schitt’s Creek, Levy returns to familiar ground here, playing a lovable, tightly wound character navigating discomfort with his signature wit.Courtesy of NetflixTaylor Ortega as MorganMorgan, Nicky’s sister, sets the entire series in motion with one very bad decision. Messy, grouchy, and rough around the edges, she can’t help but drag her family into situations they are hilariously unprepared for.Ortega first broke out through digital shorts and comedy before gaining wider recognition as a correspondent on The Daily Show. She’s appeared on shows such as Succession and Search Party, but Big Mistakes marks her first time as a series lead.Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowCourtesy of NetflixLaurie Metcalf as LindaLaurie Metcalf brings an entertaining maternal energy to Big Mistakes as Linda, the siblings’ mother, whose local political campaign becomes complicated by her children’s illicit activity.Metcalf is a sitcom legend, having played unforgettable roles in Roseanne, The Conners, and The Big Bang Theory.What to Read NextCourtesy of NetflixBoran Kuzum as YusufBoran Kuzum plays Yuzuf, the store owner whose necklace Morgan steals. After recognizing Morgan, he pulls the siblings into assisting in increasingly shady deals.Kuzum has built his career in Turkish television and film, with Big Mistakes marking his first international series debut.Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowCourtesy of NetflixJack Innanen as MaxMax is Morgan’s overly eager boyfriend, already thinking about marriage long before she is. His intensity raises more questions than answers, and adds another layer of awkward tension to an already unstable situation.Jack Innanen is known for his deadpan delivery and offbeat comedic style, having starred in FX’s Adults.Courtesy of NetflixAbby Quinn as NatalieNatalie is Nicky and Morgan’s poised youngest sibling, caught between her mother’s political ambitions and her family’s unraveling situation. As she helps manage Linda’s campaign, she’s inevitably pulled in deeper to their troubles.Abby Quinn first gained attention in Mad About You and has since carved out a niche in character-driven projects like Knock at the Cabin (2023) and Hell of a Summer (2023).Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowCourtesy of NetflixJacob Gutierrez as TareqTareq, Nicky’s boyfriend, is a local handyman, balancing Nicky’s public role as a pastor with their private relationship.Big Mistakes marks Gutierrez’s shift to television, following his breakout role as the lead in Aladdin on Broadway. He told Out Magazine he landed the role through his niece, who was interning at a casting agency. She sent him the part after realizing he was a perfect fit.Courtesy of NetflixElizabeth Perkins as AnnetteAnnette is Max’s devoted mother, deeply rooted in the community as a local real estate agent.Elizabeth Perkins brings decades of experience to the role, with recent appearances in The Housemaid (2025), The Afterparty, Minx, and This Is Us. She is perhaps best known for her performances in the TV show Weeds, as well as films including About Last Night... (1986), Big (1988), and Miracle on 34th Street (1994).Advertisement - Continue Reading BelowSPENCER PAZERMark Ivanir as IvanIvan is Yusuf’s boss, whom Nicky and Morgan are eventually forced to confront.Fluent in six languages, Mark Ivanir is a Soviet-born Israeli actor. His acting credits include Schindler’s List, Mr. & Mrs. Smith, The Good Shepherd, The Terminal, and more. More recently, he appeared as Dr. Wasserman in Emilia Pérez.SPENCER PAZERDarren Goldstein as Tom DonaldsonTom Donaldson is a prominent figure in the community and Linda’s primary opponent in the local political campaign.Darren Goldstein is recognized for his roles in Ozark and The Affair.",
